.TH BOOT-R-INSTALL 8 "October 2026" "boot-r 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
boot-r-install \- install the boot.R UEFI boot manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boot-r-install
[\fB\-\-esp\fR \fIMOUNTPOINT\fR] [\fB\-\-uninstall\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copies the boot.R UEFI application to \fIEFI/bootR/\fR on the EFI System Partition and registers it with
\fBefibootmgr\fR(8) as the first boot entry. Existing boot entries are not modified. Installing the package
alone does not change the firmware; this command does.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-esp \fIMOUNTPOINT\fR
Use this mounted EFI System Partition instead of detecting one at /boot/efi, /efi or /boot.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
Delete the "boot.R" boot entry and the \fIEFI/bootR/\fR directory.
.SH NOTES
Requires root and a system booted in UEFI mode. boot.R is not signed, so Secure Boot must be disabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR efibootmgr (8)
